WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.459 --> 00:00:06.160
Speaker 1: Ladies and gentlemen, I have a
momentous bit of news for all of you.

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:11.290
I know I hope everybody is sitting down because
there is something that happened last night

00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:19.380
on the Tucker Carlson program that has absolutely
rocked the Republican primary and is completely

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:21.490
changing the dynamics.

00:00:21.490 --> 00:00:29.779
Vivek Ramaswamy has announced that he is entering
the Republican primary.

00:00:29.779 --> 00:00:31.000
I know, I know.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:33.800
I'm giving everybody time to react to this.

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:34.800
No one cares.

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:38.190
And it's really, really even Tucker Carlson
kind of seems not to care.

00:00:38.190 --> 00:00:40.250
It's it's kind of sad, to be honest.

00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:43.230
Vivek Ramaswamy is it?

00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:44.430
This is so stupid.

00:00:44.430 --> 00:00:51.850
He's an anti-woke entrepreneur and he founded
last year something called Strive Asset Management.

00:00:51.850 --> 00:00:56.340
It's an asset management firm, which on its
websites, on its website, says it seeks to

00:00:56.340 --> 00:00:58.710
restore the voices of everyday citizens.

00:00:58.710 --> 00:01:00.210
Oh, okay.

00:01:00.210 --> 00:01:01.800
That sounds pretty, pretty cool.

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:04.090
So anyway, here he is.

00:01:04.090 --> 00:01:07.759
And it's just like a deflated balloon.

00:01:07.759 --> 00:01:10.520
Take a look at this on, you know, just a cable
host.

00:01:10.520 --> 00:01:15.220
But this is a perfect illustration of where
identity politics wind up, right when you

00:01:15.220 --> 00:01:19.100
stray from the universal principles that bind
us all under the same rules.

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:20.100
Speaker 3: Exactly.

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:24.479
I mean, we are in the middle of this national
identity crisis, Tucker, where we have celebrated

00:01:24.479 --> 00:01:27.299
our diversity and our differences for so long.

00:01:27.299 --> 00:01:28.800
Yeah, we forgot all of the ways.

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:34.520
We're really just the same as Americans, bound
by a common set of ideals that set this nation

00:01:34.520 --> 00:01:36.299
into motion 250 years ago.

00:01:36.299 --> 00:01:37.299
Whoa.

00:01:37.299 --> 00:01:40.890
And that's why I'm proud to say tonight that
I am running for United States president.

00:01:40.890 --> 00:01:41.890
Wow.

00:01:41.890 --> 00:01:47.270
Those ideals in this country, those basic
rules of the road meritocracy, the idea that

00:01:47.270 --> 00:01:51.390
you get ahead in this country, not on the
color of your skin, but in the content of

00:01:51.390 --> 00:01:52.390
your character, Right.

00:01:52.390 --> 00:01:54.469
That you are allowed to speak freely.

00:01:54.469 --> 00:01:55.469
Yes.

00:01:55.469 --> 00:01:59.170
To be wrong sometimes, as long as your neighbor
gets the same courtesy in return that the

00:01:59.170 --> 00:02:02.740
people who we elect to run the government,
by the way, are the people who actually run

00:02:02.740 --> 00:02:04.100
the government.

00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:05.100
Basic rules of the road.

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:06.380
These are the things that bind us together.

00:02:06.380 --> 00:02:08.250
You and I have different shades of melanin.

00:02:08.250 --> 00:02:09.379
You know what I say.

00:02:09.379 --> 00:02:10.379
So what?

00:02:10.379 --> 00:02:15.990
Speaker 1: You know, I could have sworn that
he said different shades of shades of melon.

00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:24.720
Like, you know, Tucker is more of a honeydew
guy, whereas Vivek is really preferential

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:25.720
to cantaloupe.

00:02:25.720 --> 00:02:29.140
But I think what he's saying is different
shades of melanin, right?

00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:30.400
Like different skin color.

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:32.070
Speaker 3: That's not beautiful.

00:02:32.070 --> 00:02:33.380
That is not our strength.

00:02:33.380 --> 00:02:38.540
Our diversity is meaningless if there's nothing
greater that binds us together across that

00:02:38.540 --> 00:02:39.540
diversity.

00:02:39.540 --> 00:02:40.540
Yeah.

00:02:40.540 --> 00:02:43.180
And the reason that I'm running for president
is to revive those ideals.

00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:47.430
And I believe deep in my bones, they still
exist, that most Americans still believe in

00:02:47.430 --> 00:02:48.430
them.

00:02:48.430 --> 00:02:49.430
But we need to rediscover that.

00:02:49.430 --> 00:02:53.090
And the only way we can do it is by start
to talking openly, start talking openly again.

00:02:53.090 --> 00:02:54.090
So I'm not going.

00:02:54.090 --> 00:02:55.090
Speaker 1: To ask it.

00:02:55.090 --> 00:02:56.090
Yeah.

00:02:56.090 --> 00:02:57.090
Really a momentous thing.

00:02:57.090 --> 00:03:01.450
And then on Twitter, Vivek Ramaswamy announced
he will end affirmative action, tweeting,

00:03:01.450 --> 00:03:07.409
quote, As US president, as US president, I
will end federally mandated affirmative action,

00:03:07.409 --> 00:03:08.409
full stop.

00:03:08.409 --> 00:03:14.230
I will repeal Lyndon Johnson's Executive Order
11 to 46, which mandates race based quotas.

00:03:14.230 --> 00:03:17.180
Every Republican since Johnson had the opportunity
to do it.

00:03:17.180 --> 00:03:18.940
I'll do it on day one without apology.

00:03:18.940 --> 00:03:20.819
Well, he won't do it and it won't be day one.

00:03:20.819 --> 00:03:22.959
There will be no day one.

00:03:22.959 --> 00:03:27.840
And there is just something funny about, you
know, in particular, like when somebody like

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:35.870
this announces, do you think they know that
this is a joke or do they actually sit somewhere

00:03:35.870 --> 00:03:37.320
and go, You never know.

00:03:37.320 --> 00:03:39.319
I might be able to pull this thing out.

00:03:39.319 --> 00:03:40.900
I'm just not sure.

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:46.290
But a very, very big get, as you can see for
Tucker Carlson getting this announcement on

00:03:46.290 --> 00:03:48.069
his program.

00:03:48.069 --> 00:03:54.620
And this certainly we will have to spend some
serious time figuring out how this announcement

00:03:54.620 --> 00:04:00.620
from RAMASWAMY is going to completely upend
the dynamics of the Republican primary.

00:04:00.620 --> 00:04:02.349
So stay with us for more on that.

00:04:02.349 --> 00:04:04.810
Maybe someday if it becomes a real thing.

00:04:04.810 --> 00:04:07.620
We're going to take a quick break and much
more to discuss.

00:04:07.620 --> 00:04:09.110
I'm very much glad you're with us today.

